            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-84243-glibc",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-84243 medium vulnerability for glibc package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in glibc. The library's localization functions fail to properly sanitize directory traversal characters within the LANGUAGE environment variable. A local attacker capable of setting this variable across trust boundaries can force a target program to load a malicious translation file from an arbitrary filesystem location. This issue can lead to arbitrary code execution under the privileges of the running application or cause an application crash, resulting in a denial of service (DoS)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-84243",
