            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53615-libblkid",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-53615 high vulnerability for libblkid package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in util-linux. An integer overflow vulnerability in the partition parsing library (libblkid) fails to properly enforce boundary checks on extended partition entries. A local attacker could exploit this flaw by presenting a crafted disk image or removable storage device for probing, causing false partition boundaries to be reported that overlap the Master Boot Record (MBR). This directly compromises the integrity of reported disk partition metadata and may result in unintended data corruption if downstream system tools act on the incorrect layout."
              },
