            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11850-krb5-libs",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11850 medium vulnerability for krb5-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An integer underflow vulnerability was found in MIT krb5 in the berval2tl_data() function in plugins/kdb/ldap/libkdb_ldap/ldap_principal2.c. The function performs an unsigned subtraction (bv_len - 2) without a prior bounds check. When bv_len is 0 or 1, the subtraction wraps to a large value which is then truncated to uint16_t, yielding 0xFFFE (65534) or 0xFFFF (65535). The subsequent malloc succeeds and memcpy reads up to 65534 bytes from a 0-1 byte buffer, resulting in a heap out-of-bounds read.\nThe attack vector involves a malicious or compromised LDAP KDB backend returning a krbExtraData attribute with bv_len \u003c 2, triggering the underflow when the KDC or kadmind reads principal data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-11850",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11850\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: krb5-libs\nVersion: 1.21.3-11.el10_3.2\nFix Version: \nType: rpm\nLocation: /usr/lib/sysimage/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite\nData Namespace: redhat:distro:redhat:10\nLink: [CVE-2026-11850](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-11850)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11850**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | krb5-libs  | 1.21.3-11.el10_3.2  |   | rpm  | /usr/lib/sysimage/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite  | redhat:distro:redhat:10  | [CVE-2026-11850](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-11850)  |\n"
