              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-97399 low vulnerability for glibc package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in glibc. In builds optimized for specific hardware architectures, the string comparison function strncasecmp may read one byte beyond the boundary of the provided input string. An attacker capable of passing controlled strings that end at the edge of a memory page could trigger an invalid memory access and crash the application, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS)."
