              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GnuTLS. The certificate verification process fails to properly reject end-entity digital certificates containing contradictory Key Usage (KU) and Extended Key Usage (EKU) extensions, which define the permitted cryptographic operations of a certificate. A remote attacker could exploit this flaw by presenting a specially crafted certificate to bypass validation controls, potentially resulting in information disclosure."
